[% META
   title = "HDRY Filament Dryer — 3D project import playbook"
   description = "Step-by-step plan to bring a downloaded 3D project (HDRY filament dryer) into File Manager, inventory BOM, provider invoice + monthly support, and the print queue. This dryer pack is the test scenario; the same playbook is the knowledge base for the next project."
   roles = "admin,developer"
   TemplateType = "Documentation"
   category = "3d-printing,planning,import,internal-build"
   page_version = "0.2"
   last_updated = "Wed Aug 19 2026"
   site_specific = "false"
   project_id   = "272"
   project_code = "DRYER-INT"
%]
[% PageVersion = 'Documentation/DryerProjectImportPlan.tt,v 0.2 2026/08/19 hermes-agent Exp - HDRY test scenario + File Manager + AP invoice + queue + KB playbook; real project 272' %]
[% IF c.session.debug_mode == 1 %]
    [% PageVersion %]
[% END %]

<div class="container">
    [% INCLUDE 'admin/documentation/_doc_header.tt'
        page_title   = 'HDRY Filament Dryer — 3D project import playbook'
        site_name    = site_name
        user_role    = user_role
        last_updated = last_updated
        page_name    = page_name
        doc_project_id   = project_id
        doc_project_code = project_code %]

    <div class="doc-warning">
        <p class="doc-body"><strong>Correction (2026-08-19):</strong> v0.1 of this plan cited projects
        <code>#14–#18</code> as DRYER-INT. Those IDs are <em>not</em> the dryer — live
        <code>/api/projects</code> shows #14 HelpDesk, #15 Site Setup, #16 User, #17 File Management.
        The dryer project was never created on the primary Ency. This v0.2 uses the real rows created
        via the API: parent
        <a href="[% c.uri_for('/project/details') %]?project_id=272" class="doc-link">#272 DRYER-INT</a>
        under
        <a href="[% c.uri_for('/project/details') %]?project_id=206" class="doc-link">#206 3DPRINT</a>.</p>
    </div>

    <div id="toc" class="row doc-toc">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 class="doc-h2">Quick Navigation</h2>
            <p class="doc-muted">Jump to section:</p>
            <div class="doc-navrow">
                <a href="#overview" class="doc-navlink">Overview</a>
                <a href="#playbook" class="doc-navlink">Playbook</a>
                <a href="#pack" class="doc-navlink">Downloads pack</a>
                <a href="#what-exists" class="doc-navlink">What exists</a>
                <a href="#data-model" class="doc-navlink">Data model</a>
                <a href="#invoice" class="doc-navlink">Invoice + subscription</a>
                <a href="#queue" class="doc-navlink">Queue</a>
                <a href="#deps" class="doc-navlink">Cross-plan deps</a>
                <a href="#phases" class="doc-navlink">Phases</a>
                <a href="#decisions" class="doc-navlink">Decisions</a>
                <a href="#project-tracking" class="doc-navlink">Project Tracking</a>
                <a href="#see-also" class="doc-navlink">See Also</a>
            </div>
            <p class="doc-backtop"><a href="#toc">&#8593; Back to Top</a></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 id="overview" class="doc-h2">1. Overview</h2>
            <p class="doc-body">This is the <strong>test scenario</strong> for bringing a new 3D project into Comserv:
            you downloaded the HDRY System V3 filament-dryer files (3MF, PDF, zip, license, provider invoice)
            into <code>~/Downloads</code>. The goal is not just this dryer — it is a
            <strong>repeatable playbook</strong> so the next pack can go Downloads → File Manager →
            in-house models → inventory BOM → provider AP invoice + monthly support → print queue
            without rediscovering the path.</p>
            <p class="doc-body">The dryer itself is an <strong>internal build (not for sale)</strong>:
            parent assembly hidden from shop, parts printable in-house, stock-in on each completed job.</p>
            <div class="doc-info">
                <p class="doc-body"><strong>Assumptions (correct me if wrong):</strong>
                provider is CC3D / HDRY (license PDF in Downloads);
                Invoice-1981891.pdf is the files purchase;
                monthly support is a separate recurring AP cost, not a shop subscription;
                first print is a subset of the pack, not every 3MF at once;
                work runs on the 3d worktree (:4003) for printing_3d code and uses live Ency via the app API.</p>
            </div>
            <p class="doc-backtop"><a href="#toc">&#8593; Back to Top</a></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 id="playbook" class="doc-h2">2. Knowledge-base playbook (how to start printing)</h2>
            <p class="doc-body">Copy this sequence for the next project. Routes verified against
            <code>Controller::File</code>, <code>Controller::3d</code>, <code>Controller::Inventory</code>,
            <code>Controller::Documentation</code> (<code>view :Path('/Documentation') :Args(1)</code>),
            <code>Controller::Project</code> (<code>details</code> reads <code>project_id</code>),
            <code>Controller::Todo</code> (<code>/todo/details?record_id=</code>).</p>
            <table class="doc-table">
                <tr>
                    <th class="doc-th">Step</th>
                    <th class="doc-th">Where</th>
                    <th class="doc-th">Done when</th>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td class="doc-td">1. Catalog the download</td>
                    <td class="doc-td">Workstation <code>~/Downloads</code> — list 3MF/STL/PDF/ZIP/invoice/license; drop duplicate copies</td>
                    <td class="doc-td">In-scope file list written on the project</td>
                </tr>
                <tr class="doc-tr-alt">
                    <td class="doc-td">2. Land files in File Manager</td>
                    <td class="doc-td"><a href="[% c.uri_for('/file/admin_browser') %]" class="doc-link">/file/admin_browser</a>
                    → upload (<a href="[% c.uri_for('/file/upload_file') %]" class="doc-link">/file/upload_file</a>)
                    into an NFS project folder → <code>db_import_file</code> so each has a <code>files.id</code></td>
                    <td class="doc-td">No hardcoded Downloads path in the importer</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td class="doc-td">3. Parent assembly item</td>
                    <td class="doc-td"><a href="[% c.uri_for('/Inventory/item/add') %]" class="doc-link">/Inventory/item/add</a>
                    — <code>show_in_shop=0</code>, <code>list_in_marketplace=0</code>, <code>is_assemblable=1</code>, <code>item_origin=3d_printed</code></td>
                    <td class="doc-td">Hidden from <a href="[% c.uri_for('/shop') %]" class="doc-link">/shop</a></td>
                </tr>
                <tr class="doc-tr-alt">
                    <td class="doc-td">4. Models + BOM</td>
                    <td class="doc-td">Each printable part → <code>printing_3d_models</code> + child item +
                    <a href="[% c.uri_for('/Inventory/bom/add') %]" class="doc-link">/Inventory/bom/add</a> line.
                    Staff-prep: review mesh before queue.</td>
                    <td class="doc-td">Visible on <a href="[% c.uri_for('/3d/models') %]" class="doc-link">/3d/models</a>
                    and <a href="[% c.uri_for('/Inventory/bom/list') %]" class="doc-link">/Inventory/bom/list</a></td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td class="doc-td">5. Provider invoice</td>
                    <td class="doc-td">Supplier at <a href="[% c.uri_for('/Inventory/suppliers') %]" class="doc-link">/Inventory/suppliers</a>;
                    AP invoice at <a href="[% c.uri_for('/Inventory/invoice/new') %]" class="doc-link">/Inventory/invoice/new</a>
                    (files purchase). Attach the PDF from File Manager.</td>
                    <td class="doc-td">Draft/posted row on <a href="[% c.uri_for('/Inventory/invoice') %]" class="doc-link">/Inventory/invoice</a></td>
                </tr>
                <tr class="doc-tr-alt">
                    <td class="doc-td">6. Monthly support</td>
                    <td class="doc-td">Wanted: recurring AP. Today only <code>auto_pay</code> exists — see INV-R1
                    <a href="[% c.uri_for('/todo/details') %]?record_id=2190" class="doc-link">todo #2190</a> on #207.
                    Workaround until then: recurring reminder todo + amount in project comments.</td>
                    <td class="doc-td">Either a real recurring AP or an honest workaround</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td class="doc-td">7. Queue and print</td>
                    <td class="doc-td"><a href="[% c.uri_for('/3d/queue') %]" class="doc-link">/3d/queue</a>
                    — jobs <code>source_type=project</code>. Complete via
                    <a href="[% c.uri_for('/3d/queue_print') %]" class="doc-link">/3d/queue_print</a>.
                    Filament txn refs <code>3D-JOB-{id}</code>.</td>
                    <td class="doc-td">First job completed; child stock &gt; 0</td>
                </tr>
            </table>
            <p class="doc-body">The same steps are mirrored (shorter) on
            <a href="[% c.uri_for('/Documentation/3d_printing') %]" class="doc-link">/Documentation/3d_printing</a>
            so operators do not have to open this plan to start a print.</p>
            <p class="doc-backtop"><a href="#toc">&#8593; Back to Top</a></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 id="pack" class="doc-h2">3. This test pack (Downloads, 2026-08-19)</h2>
            <p class="doc-body">Found on the workstation. Duplicates in parentheses are copies — ingest one.</p>
            <table class="doc-table">
                <tr>
                    <th class="doc-th">File</th>
                    <th class="doc-th">Role</th>
                </tr>
                <tr><td class="doc-td"><code>023022_HDRY_System_V3__Module_1.3mf</code></td><td class="doc-td">Printable module 1</td></tr>
                <tr class="doc-tr-alt"><td class="doc-td"><code>023030_HDRY_System_V3__Module_2.3mf</code></td><td class="doc-td">Printable module 2</td></tr>
                <tr><td class="doc-td"><code>023037_HDRY_System_V3__Doors.3mf</code></td><td class="doc-td">Doors</td></tr>
                <tr class="doc-tr-alt"><td class="doc-td"><code>023113_HDRY_System_V3__Dryer__Extras.3mf</code></td><td class="doc-td">Extras</td></tr>
                <tr><td class="doc-td"><code>110520_HDRY_System_V3__AMS__Hydra__Rollers.3mf</code> (+ two copies)</td><td class="doc-td">AMS/Hydra rollers — keep one</td></tr>
                <tr class="doc-tr-alt"><td class="doc-td"><code>141256_HDry_Lite___Desicant_box__Print_File.3mf</code></td><td class="doc-td">Desiccant box (good first print)</td></tr>
                <tr><td class="doc-td"><code>110529_HDRY_System__Upgrade_2.zip</code></td><td class="doc-td">Upgrade pack — inspect then import selected</td></tr>
                <tr class="doc-tr-alt"><td class="doc-td"><code>192244_HDRY_System__Assembly_Manual.pdf</code> (+ copy)</td><td class="doc-td">Build instructions — attach to parent item</td></tr>
                <tr><td class="doc-td"><code>131051_CC3D_PROJECTS_3D_FILE_LICENSE_AGREEMENT.pdf</code></td><td class="doc-td">License — attach to supplier / project</td></tr>
                <tr class="doc-tr-alt"><td class="doc-td"><code>Invoice-1981891.pdf</code></td><td class="doc-td">Provider invoice for the files — AP source doc</td></tr>
            </table>
            <p class="doc-body">3MF is a ZIP of meshes. <code>_parse_stl</code> will not give volume/weight until
            we extract STL objects (decision D1). The 3d controller already accepts <code>file_type=3mf</code>.</p>
            <p class="doc-backtop"><a href="#toc">&#8593; Back to Top</a></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 id="what-exists" class="doc-h2">4. What already exists (reuse, do not rebuild)</h2>
            <table class="doc-table">
                <tr><th class="doc-th">Need</th><th class="doc-th">Existing</th></tr>
                <tr><td class="doc-td">File Manager</td><td class="doc-td"><code>Controller::File</code> — <code>/file/admin_browser</code>, <code>/file/upload_file</code>, <code>/file/db_import_file</code>, <code>/file/fs_upload_tree</code>, <code>/file/file_picker</code></td></tr>
                <tr class="doc-tr-alt"><td class="doc-td">Models / jobs / printers</td><td class="doc-td"><code>printing_3d_models</code>, <code>printing_3d_jobs</code>, <code>printing_3d_printers</code> + <code>Controller::3d</code></td></tr>
                <tr><td class="doc-td">BOM + stock</td><td class="doc-td"><code>inventory_item_bom</code>, <code>inventory_items</code>, <code>inventory_transactions</code> via <code>_inventory_transaction</code></td></tr>
                <tr class="doc-tr-alt"><td class="doc-td">Provider AP invoice</td><td class="doc-td"><code>inventory_supplier_invoices</code> + <code>/Inventory/invoice</code> (owned by Inventory, not 3d)</td></tr>
                <tr><td class="doc-td">Monthly subscription</td><td class="doc-td"><strong>Gap.</strong> Invoice has <code>auto_pay</code> only. Raised as INV-R1 #2190 on #207.</td></tr>
                <tr class="doc-tr-alt"><td class="doc-td">Parent 3D project</td><td class="doc-td">#38 3dPrinting → #206 3DPRINT → phases #207 INV, #208 File Mgmt, #209 Sales</td></tr>
            </table>
            <p class="doc-body">No new tables for the dryer import. Automation (when built) is a <em>new</em>
            thin <code>Controller::ProjectImport</code> + <code>Util::ProjectImport</code> — do not grow
            <code>3d.pm</code>. Until that exists, this test scenario is executed with the live UI
            (File Manager + Inventory + /3d/queue) so we learn the playbook from a real pass.</p>
            <p class="doc-backtop"><a href="#toc">&#8593; Back to Top</a></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 id="data-model" class="doc-h2">5. Data model for the dryer</h2>
            <ul class="doc-body">
                <li><strong>Parent item</strong> — HDRY System V3, sku <code>INT-HDRY-001</code>, hidden, assemblable.</li>
                <li><strong>Each printable part</strong> — <code>printing_3d_models</code> (<code>source=project_import</code>, <code>tags=project:hdry</code>, <code>file_id</code> → FileManager) + child <code>inventory_items</code> + BOM line.</li>
                <li><strong>PDFs</strong> — FileManager rows; assembly manual on the parent; license on the supplier.</li>
                <li><strong>Jobs</strong> — <code>printing_3d_jobs</code> <code>source_type=project</code>, <code>source_item_id</code>=parent item, qty = BOM qty.</li>
            </ul>
            <p class="doc-backtop"><a href="#toc">&#8593; Back to Top</a></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 id="invoice" class="doc-h2">6. Invoice for the files + monthly support</h2>
            <p class="doc-body">This is Inventory/Accounting work consumed by the 3d project — not a second
            invoice stack. Use the existing supplier-invoice UI.</p>
            <ul class="doc-body">
                <li>Create/find supplier (CC3D / HDRY) at <a href="[% c.uri_for('/Inventory/suppliers') %]" class="doc-link">/Inventory/suppliers</a>.</li>
                <li>New AP invoice at <a href="[% c.uri_for('/Inventory/invoice/new') %]" class="doc-link">/Inventory/invoice/new</a>
                    using Invoice-1981891 as the source document (line = digital files / license, not a shop SKU).</li>
                <li>Monthly support: <strong>blocked</strong> on INV-R1
                    <a href="[% c.uri_for('/todo/details') %]?record_id=2190" class="doc-link">#2190</a>
                    until Inventory adds recurrence. Workaround: reminder todo + amount on project #272.</li>
            </ul>
            <p class="doc-backtop"><a href="#toc">&#8593; Back to Top</a></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 id="queue" class="doc-h2">7. Print queue setup (quick start)</h2>
            <ol class="doc-body">
                <li>Confirm printers at <a href="[% c.uri_for('/3d/printers') %]" class="doc-link">/3d/printers</a> and filament stock.</li>
                <li>Staff-prep the first mesh (orient / scale / supports). Do not auto-print an unreviewed 3MF.</li>
                <li>Create jobs → <a href="[% c.uri_for('/3d/queue') %]" class="doc-link">/3d/queue</a>.</li>
                <li>Complete via <a href="[% c.uri_for('/3d/queue_print') %]" class="doc-link">/3d/queue_print</a>. Expect filament <code>issue</code> and a <code>receive</code> of the finished child part (extend job-completion if receive is still filament-only — that hook is 3d-owned).</li>
            </ol>
            <p class="doc-backtop"><a href="#toc">&#8593; Back to Top</a></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 id="deps" class="doc-h2">8. Cross-plan dependency register</h2>
            <p class="doc-body">Raise, do not absorb. 3d branch does not patch File.pm or Inventory.pm for these.</p>
            <table class="doc-table">
                <tr><th class="doc-th">Req</th><th class="doc-th">Need</th><th class="doc-th">Why blocked</th><th class="doc-th">Raised on</th></tr>
                <tr>
                    <td class="doc-td">INV-R1</td>
                    <td class="doc-td">Recurring monthly supplier support invoice</td>
                    <td class="doc-td"><code>inventory_supplier_invoices</code> has <code>auto_pay</code> only</td>
                    <td class="doc-td"><a href="[% c.uri_for('/todo/details') %]?record_id=2190" class="doc-link">todo #2190</a> / project #207</td>
                </tr>
                <tr class="doc-tr-alt">
                    <td class="doc-td">FM-R1</td>
                    <td class="doc-td">Optional batch folder ingest</td>
                    <td class="doc-td">Upload is per-file; pack is ~10 files — workable by hand for this test</td>
                    <td class="doc-td">Defer unless P2 proves painful; then raise on #208</td>
                </tr>
            </table>
            <p class="doc-backtop"><a href="#toc">&#8593; Back to Top</a></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 id="phases" class="doc-h2">9. Phases (sub-projects) and gates</h2>
            <p class="doc-body">Each phase is a sub-project of #272. Work todos live under that phase. Open the
            phase log before editing code that implements it.</p>
            <table class="doc-table">
                <tr><th class="doc-th">Phase</th><th class="doc-th">Project</th><th class="doc-th">GATE</th></tr>
                <tr>
                    <td class="doc-td">P0 Role + deps</td>
                    <td class="doc-td"><a href="[% c.uri_for('/project/details') %]?project_id=273" class="doc-link">#273 DRYER-P0</a></td>
                    <td class="doc-td"><strong>GATE 0</strong> — owners named from live evidence; INV-R1 raised</td>
                </tr>
                <tr class="doc-tr-alt">
                    <td class="doc-td">P1 Catalog Downloads</td>
                    <td class="doc-td"><a href="[% c.uri_for('/project/details') %]?project_id=274" class="doc-link">#274 DRYER-P1</a></td>
                    <td class="doc-td"><strong>GATE 1</strong> — de-duplicated in-scope list on #272</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td class="doc-td">P2 File Manager</td>
                    <td class="doc-td"><a href="[% c.uri_for('/project/details') %]?project_id=275" class="doc-link">#275 DRYER-P2</a></td>
                    <td class="doc-td"><strong>GATE 2</strong> — every in-scope file has <code>files.id</code></td>
                </tr>
                <tr class="doc-tr-alt">
                    <td class="doc-td">P3 Models + BOM</td>
                    <td class="doc-td"><a href="[% c.uri_for('/project/details') %]?project_id=276" class="doc-link">#276 DRYER-P3</a></td>
                    <td class="doc-td"><strong>GATE 3</strong> — parent + children + BOM + models visible in-app</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td class="doc-td">P4 Invoice + support</td>
                    <td class="doc-td"><a href="[% c.uri_for('/project/details') %]?project_id=277" class="doc-link">#277 DRYER-P4</a></td>
                    <td class="doc-td"><strong>GATE 4</strong> — files invoice posted; subscription real or workaround documented</td>
                </tr>
                <tr class="doc-tr-alt">
                    <td class="doc-td">P5 Queue + first print</td>
                    <td class="doc-td"><a href="[% c.uri_for('/project/details') %]?project_id=278" class="doc-link">#278 DRYER-P5</a></td>
                    <td class="doc-td"><strong>GATE 5</strong> — jobs on /3d/queue; one completed with stock-in</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td class="doc-td">P6 Knowledge base</td>
                    <td class="doc-td"><a href="[% c.uri_for('/project/details') %]?project_id=279" class="doc-link">#279 DRYER-P6</a></td>
                    <td class="doc-td"><strong>GATE 6</strong> — 3d_printing.tt playbook matches what actually worked</td>
                </tr>
            </table>
            <p class="doc-backtop"><a href="#toc">&#8593; Back to Top</a></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 id="decisions" class="doc-h2">10. Open decisions</h2>
            <table class="doc-table">
                <tr><th class="doc-th">#</th><th class="doc-th">Decision</th><th class="doc-th">Resolution</th></tr>
                <tr>
                    <td class="doc-td">D1</td>
                    <td class="doc-td">3MF handling</td>
                    <td class="doc-td">OPEN — extract STL objects for <code>_parse_stl</code> vs register 3mf and skip volume. Default assumed: extract for first-print parts only.</td>
                </tr>
                <tr class="doc-tr-alt">
                    <td class="doc-td">D2</td>
                    <td class="doc-td">First print set</td>
                    <td class="doc-td">OPEN — default assumed: HDry Lite desiccant box + Module 1, not the full dryer.</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td class="doc-td">D3</td>
                    <td class="doc-td">Monthly support</td>
                    <td class="doc-td">OPEN — wait for INV-R1 vs reminder-todo workaround. Default: workaround so P4 can close.</td>
                </tr>
                <tr class="doc-tr-alt">
                    <td class="doc-td">D4</td>
                    <td class="doc-td">Import automation vs manual first pass</td>
                    <td class="doc-td">OPEN — default: manual UI pass first (this is the test scenario that writes the playbook); automation is a follow-on under the same project, not a blocker to printing.</td>
                </tr>
            </table>
            <p class="doc-backtop"><a href="#toc">&#8593; Back to Top</a></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 id="project-tracking" class="doc-h2">Project Tracking</h2>
            <p class="doc-body">
                Owning project:
                <a href="[% c.uri_for('/project/details') %]?project_id=272" class="doc-link">#272 (DRYER-INT)</a>
                — parent:
                <a href="[% c.uri_for('/project/details') %]?project_id=206" class="doc-link">#206 (3DPRINT)</a>
                — grandparent:
                <a href="[% c.uri_for('/project/details') %]?project_id=38" class="doc-link">#38 (3dPrinting)</a>.
                Todos:
                <a href="[% c.uri_for('/todo') %]?project_id=272" class="doc-link">filter by #272</a>.
                All projects:
                <a href="[% c.uri_for('/project') %]" class="doc-link">/project</a>.
            </p>
            <table class="doc-table">
                <tr>
                    <th class="doc-th">Phase / Sub-project</th>
                    <th class="doc-th">Todos (phase → step → gate)</th>
                    <th class="doc-th">Gate / Done when</th>
